    "created_at": "2017-08-16T16:00:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T16:00:29Z",
    "body": "I guess you are talking about the HTMLCollection case. Otherwise it is indeed specific as it returns specific objects in the DOM tree, which always maintain their identity over time.\r\n\r\nThere exists some text for this for e.g. getElementsByName:\r\n\r\n> When the method is invoked on a Document object again with the same argument, the user agent may return the same as the object returned by the earlier call. In other cases, a new NodeList object must be returned.\r\n\r\nBut I guess it did not makes its way to the named getters.\r\n\r\nI wonder whether we want to have a tighter requirement that you must always return the same value. I wonder if that's even true in implementations though, e.g. maybe they clear their map of name -> HTMLCollections every once in a while (such as on heavy document mutation).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
