    "created_at": "2017-08-16T17:56:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T17:56:47Z",
    "body": "In Gecko right now we don't particularly match the spec at all, but insofar as we do, we have a single list that's allocated once for the document when it's first needed and never deallocated.  I think we should either spec that it's always the same value or always a new one -- I don't think UAs should be allowed to sometimes return a new one if they feel like it.",
